    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "What do you mean by \"pink pit mist\"? I’ve never heard of that in textile production. And checking the surroundings for drafts—we've already checked the AC and the ventilation, and the heat is staying consistent in the zone. \n\nIt’s not just small spots, it’s like specific sections of the design just drop out mid-press. It is so frustrating because it feels like something is physically pulling the color away from the paper during the heat cycle. Is there any chemical reason why pigment would just fail to bond and effectively disappear?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
